lock__body_markdown_content__html amp-unmask" data-v-033ac052=3D""><p>Follo=
wing our initial exploit, we can see how this vulnerability could also lead=
 to a Denial of Service (DoS) condition. By injecting JavaScript, such as a=
n infinite <code>while</code> loop, we could cause the database to hang.</p=
>
<p>This is possible because MongoDB's <code>$where</code> operator allows t=
he execution of JavaScript as part of a query. Our Rust application was vul=
nerable because we failed to sanitize the user's input; the <code>search_qu=
ery</code> string was used directly without any validation.</p>
<p>Let's examine how the vulnerable Rust code in our <code>vulnerable_searc=
h</code> handler allowed this to happen:</p>
