"">Key Takeaways</h3><div class=3D"block__body_markdown_content__html amp-u=
nmask" data-v-033ac052=3D""><ul>
<li>NoSQL databases are vulnerable to injection vulnerabilities. The princi=
ples of trusting user input are the same as with traditional SQL databases.=
</li>
<li>NoSQL injections can be more dangerous than SQL injections. As we've se=
en with the <code>$where</code> operator, some attacks can lead to code exe=
cution on the server, not just data retrieval.</li>
<li>Remediate NoSQL injections by validating and sanitizing user-supplied i=
nput. In Rust, this is best achieved by leveraging the strong type system (=
like using <code>web::Form&lt;User&gt;</code>) and building safe queries wi=
th BSON macros (<code>doc!</code>) rather than formatting raw strings. Avoi=
d dangerous operators whenever possible.</li>
</ul>
